  m_IsActive: 1
--- !u!114 &290665154
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 290665153}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 51bf743a7b9a61e409329faa416e2f81, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Ronin7.World::Ronin7.World.Story.DialoguePlayer
  lines:
  - speaker: Vess
    text: Don't. Don't you tell me you're the champion of the galaxy. I am not buying
      it.
    seconds: 9
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 2090b89d50f478844b93d8f20a91656b, type: 3}
  - speaker: Ronin-7
    text: I was built to be that. I'm not it anymore, and I'm trying to pay for what
      I was. Let me put down the thing the Dominion's building, and then my life's
      yours.
    seconds: 21
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: c1527e0f8b2b0e94db5a2ef34d58c661, type: 3}
  - speaker: Vess
    text: Then you carry them too. All of them, mine and his and yours, every name
      in that rack. You don't get to die until every last one has been spoken out
      loud to the whole galaxy. That's a longer sentence than the one I came down
      here to give you, and it's heavier, and you'll wear it every day until it's
      done. That's worse than killing you. Good. Take the blade. If I'm putting it
      down, I'm putting it in the hand that has the most names to answer for. Don't
      make me regret the worst mercy I've ever shown.
    seconds: 24
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 466d5cb9de60eec4ba3e73dc7d1466d4, type: 3}
  - speaker: Ronin-7
    text: I'll wear it. Every name, out loud, until the dark gives all of them back.
      That's the work anyway, Vess. You didn't sentence me to anything I wasn't already
      carrying down this hole. But I'll carry yours by name now, with the rest. Take
      a berth on my ship. The strays read the dead together up there. There's room
      for one more.
    seconds: 16
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: bbdd2bdf8bfb51d4088017e341ef07f1, type: 3}
  - speaker: Gryph
    text: A year ago I'd have called that the stupidest thing I ever watched a man
      do, taking a live blade off someone who came to kill him. I threw in with him
      over the same kind of stupid. Raider. I don't know your war. But I know that
      choice when I see it twice in one day. You'll do.
    seconds: 13
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 44fdd44e6b5fe0b4aba79ecd20e19caa, type: 3}
  - speaker: Echo
    text: She spared you, Cipher. Took the killing blow and chose not to land it.
      Do you feel the size of that. Every keeper down here this whole saga, Vane,
      Sever, every leashed brother of every make before yours, the only mercy on
      offer was a clean death. And this one, who had every right in the galaxy to
      take your life, looked at the names and put the blade in your hand instead.
      That's the chapter, right there. We've been putting down the cages that came
      before you all the way down. She's the first one that chose to spare you back.
    seconds: 19
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 0aa1c92c6ab62484c866a1add282713c, type: 3}
  textMesh: {fileID: 1593870992}
  panelRoot: {fileID: 1349131099}
  audioSource: {fileID: 290665155}
  billboardToCamera: 1
  playOnStart: 0
  followDistance: 1.5
  followVerticalOffset: -0.55
  followLerp: 12
  maxCharsPerLine: 36
  autoAdvanceBeat: 0.45
  advanceAction: {fileID: -3790664182463143341, guid: d5a2441a867c2484c888f3631c932d48, type: 3}
