  - component: {fileID: 404296012}
  - component: {fileID: 404296011}
  - component: {fileID: 404296010}
  m_Layer: 0
  m_Name: Dialogue_Beat3_Reading
  m_TagString: Untagged
  m_Icon: {fileID: 0}
  m_NavMeshLayer: 0
  m_StaticEditorFlags: 0
  m_IsActive: 1
--- !u!114 &404296010
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 404296009}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 51bf743a7b9a61e409329faa416e2f81, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Ronin7.World::Ronin7.World.Story.DialoguePlayer
  lines:
  - speaker: Cassie-04
    text: 'All right. Watch the light. This is the part they buried a mine on top
      of so it could never be read aloud. Here they are, Cipher. Not numbers. Not
      assets. Names. The make seated in my spine is Ninja, my own generation, but
      the count I keep reaches every node and every make: every operative the Program
      ever erased, the true name they were given before they were given a serial,
      and the place they put the body after. I have been keeping this count alone
      in the cold for six years and never once been allowed to say a single one of
      them out loud to a living soul who cared. So. Where do you want to start.'
    seconds: 26
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 8764268df5b90fc4e939169b84b52ccc, type: 3}
  - speaker: Ronin-7
    text: From the start. The oldest first. Read them like they mattered, because
      somebody on my ship made me promise they would. And every name you read, I
      want the line. Were they Program. Were they a child. Were they someone like
      me.
    seconds: 12
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 6fe05d6aba48644429579b1bf5e60962, type: 3}
  - speaker: Cassie-04
    text: The oldest first. Then you'll want to sit, metaphorically, because the
      old ones are the worst. Here. This one was a teacher before they took her.
      This one was twelve. This one cut his own leash and lasted nine days before
      they filed him. This one. Cipher, half of these are children, and the other
      half are people who were children when the Program took them. You weren't an
      exception. You were a line-item. And every single one of them went into the
      dark with no one ever saying the name their mother gave them. Until now. So
      I'll keep reading, and you keep standing there taking it, because somebody
      finally should.
    seconds: 26
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 1d17d05a7e6ae81458d80f7316cde098, type: 3}
  - speaker: Echo
    text: I'm reading with you, Cipher. I can't not. Every one of these had a shadow,
      and every shadow is one of me, filed in this index like a thing in a drawer.
      There. And there. The kept I promised we'd come back for, half of them are
      in this list with a disposal-site next to the name. We didn't just find the
      count. We found the address of everyone we're trying to save. Keep listening.
      I know it's heavy. This is the heaviest thing we'll ever carry and it's also
      the only map that gets us to them.
    seconds: 19
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 4c57b0191a1e03b459304beed9a5714b, type: 3}
  - speaker: Ronin-7
    text: Find me one more. Find me mine. If everyone in this room has a name their
      mother gave them, I want to know if I had one too, before they made me a number.
    seconds: 11
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: ea78ab2451be6c644962b2a70602dcef, type: 3}
  - speaker: Cassie-04
    text: I was waiting for you to ask. I've had your file flagged since the second
      you walked in, because the index knew your face before I did. Here it is. Ronin-7.
      And. Hm. That's. Give me a moment. No. Cipher, I'm sorry. Your entry's here,
      it's the only one in the whole ledger that's sealed from the inside, locked
      at a depth even I can't read from where I'm standing. Everyone else, I can
      hand you. You, they buried twice. There's a name in there. I just can't open
      it from this room. Whatever they did to you, they didn't want it read even
      by their own clerk.
    seconds: 25
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 544fbca642638b24299983498142fcf6, type: 3}
  - speaker: Ronin-7
    text: Sealed from the inside. Of course it is. They made me the one thing in
      their own ledger even they were afraid to read back. Mark it, Cassie. Flag
      it and carry it up with the rest. Somewhere there's a room deeper than this
      one where that lock opens. I'll find it. Not today. Today we read the others.
    seconds: 14
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 2d907f2068025944da8b4dc072cfbde9, type: 3}
  - speaker: Cassie-04
    text: Then I'm not staying down here to wait for you to carry me up like the
      last of the furniture. Six years bolted to a wall, reading the dead to no one.
      I can walk, Cipher, and I can read on the move. Wherever this crew goes next,
      the ledger goes with it, and the ledger doesn't leave my spine, so that's settled.
      I'm coming with you. Now get me up out of this hole. I've got a galaxy of names
      to say out loud and I'd like to start before the next century.
    seconds: 18
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: f3039bd69eeb73d4981d42441d83e133, type: 3}
  - speaker: Ronin-7
    text: Then you're with us. Stay on Gryph's shoulder and keep reading. We climb.
    seconds: 6
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 954b835230129d049aea60ea4f9cbfdf, type: 3}
  textMesh: {fileID: 2087444443}
  panelRoot: {fileID: 16504748}
  audioSource: {fileID: 404296011}
  billboardToCamera: 1
  playOnStart: 0
  followDistance: 1.5
  followVerticalOffset: -0.55
  followLerp: 12
