--- !u!114 &1060604267
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1060604266}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 51bf743a7b9a61e409329faa416e2f81, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Ronin7.World::Ronin7.World.Story.DialoguePlayer
  lines:
  - speaker: Cassie-04
    text: Now for the part I've actually been looking forward to. Hand me that Engine
      schematic your engineer pulled out of the Tide. There. Watch what happens when
      you lay a ledger over a machine. You already know the build was split across
      my kind so no single capture gives you the whole. Here's the part you don't
      have. The cross-index in my spine knows exactly where the other two are kept.
      So. There's your target list, Cipher. Two more of me, out there in the dark,
      each a different make of the dead racked into a different node, each one a
      piece of the instructions for taking this thing apart.
    seconds: 21
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: f32a6702125a8c5448d97d4463da85d7, type: 3}
  - speaker: Morrigan
    text: I see them. Two nodes, lit against the Engine frame. Give me the first.
      There, the nearer one. That's. Cipher, that reads as a bone-canyon, a leviathan
      graveyard, and the dating on it is wrong, it's older than the Dominion, older
      than the Program's records should go. If there's an archive wrecked out there,
      it isn't filed under the Engine's construction. It's filed under the Engine's
      origin. Whatever's in that canyon goes back to where all of this started. We
      don't just have a node out there. We have the beginning of it.
    seconds: 22
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 0753005a3177fd145a163b44a58d8c11, type: 3}
  - speaker: Morrigan
    text: And the second. Deeper inside Dominion ground, not buried in the wild but
      wired into a cryo-command vault, one of their cold strongholds where they freeze
      the things they're not ready to use yet. That node's not lost, Cipher. It's
      in active custody, in the heart of their machine. The bone-canyon one we go
      and find. The cryo one we'll have to go in and take. Two more archives. Two
      more of her kind. Then the build-record's whole and the Engine comes apart.
    seconds: 20
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: dd689ab32f02aea48a9184f416a73f61, type: 3}
  - speaker: Sable
    text: I've felt them the whole time you've been down there, Cipher, the way I
      told you in the briefing. Two more, after Cassie. And now Cassie's map gives
      them a place, and I can lay my feeling over her index, and. The cryo one I
      can feel clean. Cold, locked, alive, angry. We can reach her. But the bone-canyon
      one. Listen to me. She reads wrong. Faint, and getting fainter, like a voice
      going out under deep water, like she's already half gone and doesn't know it.
      Cassie's the one we brought up breathing. The next one. I don't think she'll
      wait for us. I think I'm going to lose a sister before I ever reach her, and
      I think the canyon is where it happens.
    seconds: 26
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 624bd92e508b44f4fafffb8cc031d457, type: 3}
  - speaker: Ronin-7
    text: Then the canyon's first. If she's going out, we go to her before she does,
      not after. Cassie, lock both nodes to the map and keep the ledger reading the
      whole way. Vess, your sentence starts now, every name out loud as we go. Gryph,
      get us aboard the rig. We came down to read the dead by name and bring one
      of them up breathing. We did both. Now we do it twice more, and the next one's
      running out of time. Take us up.
    seconds: 20
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: f234894912d05fb46908410fe953ef06, type: 3}
  - speaker: Echo
    text: Up, for once, and not empty-handed. We came down for a count and we're
      climbing out with the names of everyone we ever lost, a step through walls,
      two more strays on the ship, and a target list with two pins in it. That's
      a win that walks out on its own legs, Cipher, the one I asked for. Enjoy it
      for the length of the lift-ride, because the next pin reads wrong, and Sable's
      scared, and you and I both know what it means when she's scared. We made the
      rebellion a plan today. The canyon's going to make it a race. But that's tomorrow's
      hole. Today we ride up clean.
    seconds: 24
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 9e9f69011d62f444b9e5ce495208e21a, type: 3}
  textMesh: {fileID: 164677304}
  panelRoot: {fileID: 653457028}
  audioSource: {fileID: 1060604268}
  billboardToCamera: 1
  playOnStart: 0
  followDistance: 1.5
  followVerticalOffset: -0.55
  followLerp: 12
  maxCharsPerLine: 36
  autoAdvanceBeat: 0.45
  advanceAction: {fileID: -3790664182463143341, guid: d5a2441a867c2484c888f3631c932d48, type: 3}
